# Legacy Monitor Test Scripts

These scripts exercise the deprecated `eden-monitor` utility using fake
`nvidia-smi` and `pidstat` commands. They do not test the active Prometheus
application in `app/`.

## Build

From the legacy module directory:

```bash
cd "_app [deprecated]/monitor"
make monitor
```

This creates `eden-monitor` next to `monitor.go`.

## Run the harness

From the repository root:

```bash
cd "_app [deprecated]/monitor/test"
chmod +x fake_nvidia_smi.sh fake_pidstat.sh test_job.sh
./fake_nvidia_smi.sh
./fake_pidstat.sh
env PATH="$(pwd):$PATH" ./test_job.sh
```

The two fake-tool scripts write executable shims into the test directory. The
harness starts the monitor, waits briefly, and sends it `SIGTERM`; it is a basic
manual check rather than an automated test suite. Using `env PATH=...` limits
the fake commands to this invocation, so no PATH cleanup is needed.

